<title>MOROCCO: Moroccan Treasury auction raises 931.5 mln dirhams.</title>
<headline>Moroccan Treasury auction raises 931.5 mln dirhams.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Moroccan Treasury raised 931.5 million dirhams from its weekly Treasury bill auction, Bank al-Maghrib (central bank) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Rates and amounts (in million dirhams) were accepted as follows:</p>
<p>    MATURITY	   BID  AMOUNT		INTEREST RATE</p>
<p>    13 weeks	    6	3		     7.45 pct</p>
<p>    26 weeks	  200    200		     8.40 pct</p>
<p>    52 weeks	    5	5		     9.00 pct</p>
<p>    Two years	  83     83		     9.50 pct</p>
<p>    Five years	188    188		    10.00 pct</p>
<p>    10 years	  150    150		    10.25 pct</p>
<p>    15 years	  302.5  302.5		  10.50 pct</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Total	     934.5  931.5</p>
<p>The interest rate on 13-week T-bills was lowered to 7.45 percent from 7.50 percent in the previous session, the bank said. ($1= 8.7 dirhams)</p>
<p>-- Rabat newsroom +212-7 726518</p>
</text>
